    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-match (\"possible duplicate\") detection for owner creation. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a different telephone, it's still created and flagged.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean, `possible_duplicate`) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer, `possible_duplicate_of`) columns with getters/setters, mirroring the existing `namesakeCount`/`householdId` pattern.\n\n2. **Schemas** \u2014 added the two columns to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). Existing `INSERT`s name columns explicitly, so seed data is unaffected.\n\n3. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` read-only properties to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them and MapStruct maps them by name automatically.\n\n4. **New function** `AssignPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 runs in the `POST /api/owners` pipeline after the hard-duplicate check (`EnsureUniqueIdentity`) and before `SaveOwner`. It finds an existing owner (excluding self) with a case-insensitive matching last name, an equal non-blank postcode, and a *different* telephone; on a match it sets `possibleDuplicate=true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` to the earliest matching owner's id (lowest id for determinism), otherwise sets `possibleDuplicate=false`.\n\n5. **Pipeline wiring** (`owners.POST.yml`) \u2014 inserted the `assignPossibleDuplicate` step, governed by the same transaction.\n\nThe soft-match is computed and persisted at creation time (like `namesakeCount`), so the values are stable and read back through the standard `GET /api/owners/{id}` mapper. Both the new acceptance test (`coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate`) and the full suite pass.",
